@startuml
title Names in Pi versus names in Rholang: which arrows the two signatures actually contain

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #6D28D9
  FontColor #111827
}
hide empty members

package "Pi — names are ATOMIC (languages/src/pi.rs)" as PIPKG #F8FAFC {
  class "Proc" as PI_PROC #DBEAFE {
    PZero : <latex>\to \mathrm{Proc}</latex>
    PNew : <latex>[\mathrm{Name} \to \mathrm{Proc}] \to \mathrm{Proc}</latex>
    PIn : <latex>\mathrm{Name} \times [\mathrm{Name} \to \mathrm{Proc}] \to \mathrm{Proc}</latex>
    POut : <latex>\mathrm{Name} \times \mathrm{Name} \times \mathrm{Proc} \to \mathrm{Proc}</latex>
    POutAsync : <latex>\mathrm{Name} \times \mathrm{Name} \to \mathrm{Proc}</latex>
    PPar : <latex>\mathrm{HashBag}(\mathrm{Proc}) \to \mathrm{Proc}</latex>
    PRep : <latex>\mathrm{Proc} \to \mathrm{Proc}</latex>
  }
  class "Name" as PI_NAME #FEE2E2 {
    NVar  (auto-injected)
    -- NO declared constructor --
    zero ""TermDef""s of category Name
  }
}

package "Rholang — names REFLECT processes (languages/src/rholang.rs)" as RHOPKG #F8FAFC {
  class "Proc" as RHO_PROC #DBEAFE {
    PZero, PPar, PNew, PForUser, POutput, ...
    **PDrop** : <latex>\mathrm{Name} \to \mathrm{Proc}</latex>   (:439)
  }
  class "Name" as RHO_NAME #DCFCE7 {
    NVar  (auto-injected)
    **NQuote** : <latex>\mathrm{Proc} \to \mathrm{Name}</latex>   (:854)
  }
}

PI_NAME -[#1D4ED8,thickness=2]-> PI_PROC : names OCCUR in processes\n(as subjects and objects)
PI_PROC -[#DC2626,thickness=2,dashed]-> PI_NAME : **NO SUCH ARROW**\nnothing builds a Name\nfrom a Proc

RHO_NAME -[#1D4ED8,thickness=2]-> RHO_PROC : names occur in processes...
RHO_PROC -[#15803D,thickness=2]-> RHO_NAME : ...**and** ""@(p)"" QUOTES a\nprocess INTO a name
RHO_NAME -[#15803D,thickness=2]-> RHO_PROC : ""*n"" DROPS a name\nback into a process

note bottom of PI_NAME #FEE2E2
  A Pi name can only ever be a VARIABLE — free, or bound
  by a ""PNew"" restriction or a ""PIn"" receive. The sort is
  declared (""types { Proc Name }"") but has no term former,
  so the set of closed names is EMPTY and the two sorts
  are disjoint. This is Milner's discipline exactly:
  names are atoms, distinct from processes.
end note

note bottom of RHO_NAME #DCFCE7
  The two green arrows close a CYCLE, and that cycle is
  the whole of reflection. The specification states the
  laws that govern it directly:
    ""QuoteDrop . |- (NQuote (PDrop N)) = N ;""   (:2943)
    ""Exec     . |- (PDrop (NQuote P)) ~> P;""    (:2954)
  i.e. ""@(*N) = N"" and ""*(@P) ~> P"" in surface syntax.
  Pi can state neither law, because it cannot even
  write the terms: it has no ""@"" and no ""*"".
end note

legend right
|= Arrow |= Meaning |
|<#DBEAFE> blue | a sort OCCURS in the other's constructors |
|<#DCFCE7> green | a constructor CROSSES the sorts — the reflective pair |
|<#FEE2E2> red dashed | an arrow the signature does NOT contain |
endlegend

@enduml
